ORIGINS -- where each added program came from==============================================================One line per program.  Companion to DOC/INDEX (what each program IS)and SOURCES.txt (licence and build method).Four origins, all public:  argproc_demo   argproc     EFFO forum disk 7 RICO/C/LIBSOURCE/ARGPROC  biory          rtf         EFFO forum disk 5 SPRACHEN/FORTRAN/BIORY -- RTF/68K example  creadoc        rtf         EFFO forum disk 5 SPRACHEN/FORTRAN/CREADOC  for            rtf         EFFO public-domain disk 1 CMDS -- RTF/68K driver  lnk            rtf         EFFO public-domain disk 1 CMDS -- RTF/68K link driver  lnk.org        rtf         EFFO public-domain disk 1 CMDS -- as lnk, original build  os9lib         rtf         EFFO public-domain disk 1 CMDS -- RTF/68K run-time library  rtf            rtf         EFFO public-domain disk 1 CMDS -- RTF/68K Fortran-77 (CERN)  rtfdat         rtf         EFFO public-domain disk 1 CMDS -- rtf's data module  usenet archive   a comp.sources.games / comp.sources.misc posting                   from the late 1980s, kept as an OS-9 'ar' archive                   in a personal collection.  Named <archive>.ar.  hc disk          the same collection's other half, recovered from a                   second OS-9 disk.  Its copies are often the better                   port -- ispell and xlisp only build from these.  EFFO forum disk  European Forum for OS-9 user-group disk, from the                   Microware hobbyist archive (microware.com, OSK).  microware        the same hobbyist archive's own category trees,                   taken directly rather than through a forum disk.The C source for every one of these is on this disk under SRC/<tree>/.--------------------------------------------------------------program        SRC/        origin--------------------------------------------------------------  advcom         advint      usenet archive  advint.ar  advent         adv         usenet arch